# learning-project (monorepo)

Canonical overview: [README.md](../../README.md). Learning order: [docs/LEARNING_PATH.md](../../docs/LEARNING_PATH.md). Agents: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

## Buckets

| Bucket | Path | Notes |
|--------|------|--------|
| Hub | `hub/` | Landing page + `path.mjs` (levels → stages → steps, `RETIRED` ids) + `progress.js` (localStorage, step bar, theme toggle) + `sheet.js` (Markdown renderer) + `theme/` (the one design, animations) + `scripts/` (`check-path.mjs`, `catalog.mjs`, `build-site.mjs`, `check-links.mjs`) |
| Sheets | `sheets/` | Short pages, one idea each, picture first (see `docs/STYLE.md`) |
| Drills | `drills/javascript/` | `tasks.js` / `tasks.test.js`; root **`Makefile`** → `bun test` |
| Tracks | `tracks/java/`, `tracks/computer-science/`, `tracks/architecture/`, `tracks/spring-boot/`, `tracks/ai/`, `tracks/certifications/aws-genai-pro/` | Static or markdown curricula — **one canonical home per topic** (link, don’t duplicate) |
| Projects | `projects/` | The project ladder `01`–`12` (each reuses the last skill, adds one): `README.md`, `step-by-step.md`, `starter/`, `solution/`, optional `help/`. Optional builds in `extras/` |
| Programs | `programs/code-for-cleaning/` | Slash commands in `programs/code-for-cleaning/.cursor/commands/` must **not** write task solutions |
| Learner memory | `docs/learner-memory/` | Profile schema, events, Cursor skill `learner-memory` |
| Students | `students/<student>/<subject>/exercises/exercise-NN-…/task-NN-k-…/` | Per-student exercise sheets; every task has README, `my-solution/`, `solution/`. Create via `/new-exercise`; see `students.mdc` |

## Stacks

- **`drills/javascript/`** — Plain JS unless a file already uses something else.
- **Static mini-sites** (`tracks/java/`, `tracks/computer-science/`, `tracks/architecture/`, `tracks/certifications/aws-genai-pro/`) — plain HTML/CSS/JS, no build. CS demos: run `node tracks/computer-science/scripts/verify-demos.mjs` after demo changes.
- **`tracks/spring-boot/`** — Markdown course; references live in `tracks/spring-boot/references/<area>/` (≤5 files per folder).

## Conventions

- **Plain JS** in drills and static tracks unless noted.
- **Structure:** See [structure.mdc](./structure.mdc) — max 5 files per folder, ~400-line soft cap.
- When scope spans buckets, update README / LEARNING_PATH cross-links.
- Pages follow `docs/STYLE.md`: picture → one idea → tiny example → try it → check, English, short sentences, `> [!PICTURE]` / `[!TRY]` / `[!CHECK]` boxes. Colours only from `hub/theme/tokens.css` (`--lp-*`).
- Cursor commands: students use `/next` → `/stuck` → `/check` → `/done` (rules in `tutor.mdc`, for student tasks, projects, drills, Code for Cleaning and path lessons); teachers use `/new-exercise` and `/new-content`. Do not add more commands: extend these.
- Students follow one list: `hub/path.mjs`. New content goes on the path by adding a step there (never rename a step `id`, progress is saved by id). The `path`, `students` and `catalog` regions of `hub/index.html` are generated: run `make site`, never hand-edit between their markers.
